{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "RRTMColumn",
    "description": "The RRTM radiation column that WRF builds from a model column (SUBROUTINE MM5ATM and the column-amount part of SETCOEF in phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, WRF 4.8): the NLEV model layers plus NBUF buffer layers above the model top, on the index sets `rlay` (RRTM layers, 1 = lowest, NLEV + NBUF members) and `rlev` (RRTM levels, 1 = surface, NLEV + NBUF + 1 members). MM5ATM: (1) the model part is a plain copy in the bottom-up order shared by this grid (PZ(L) = Pw(kte+1-L) undoes the top-down order of the wrapper's 1-D arrays): pz = p_e/100 hPa, tz = T_e, pavel = p/100, tavel = T for the model layers; (2) the buffer part continues the column to p = 0 in steps of deltap = 4 hPa (pz[j] = p_top - deltap (j - NLEV - 1) for the NBUF - 1 full buffer levels, then pz[NLEV+NBUF+1] = 0, so the top buffer layer is thinner) with layer pressures the level means; (3) buffer temperatures follow the MM5 standard atmosphere T_std(p) (the 60-point PPROF/TPROF table, linear in pressure, clamped to its 0.10 hPa end; template standard_atmosphere_temperature) shifted so that it is continuous at the model top, tz = T_std(pz) + (T_e[top] - T_std(p_top)), and tavel the level means; (4) the dry-air column of every layer coldry = (dp/g)(N_A/amm)/(1 + w) in molecules/cm^2 with w the water-vapour volume mixing ratio (qv amdw, floored at 1e-12 kg/kg, in the model layers; the constant 5e-6 above the model top) and amm = (1 - w) amd + w amw the moist molecular weight; (5) the scaled molecular column amounts of SETCOEF, col_x = 1e-20 coldry vmr_x for H2O, CO2 (co2vmr), N2O (n2ovmr) and CH4 (ch4vmr), all uniform above the model top except H2O, and colo2 = 0 because RRTM never fills WKL(7); (6) the longwave cloud optical depth of the model layers, taucloud = abcw CLWP + abice CIWP + abrn PLWP + absn PIWP with the paths in g/m^2 (CLWP = rho qc dz, the ice path likewise, and the (rho q)^0.75 rain and snow paths), 0 above the model top, and the layer cloud fraction cldfrac = cldfra forced to 1 where taucloud > 0.01 and 0 above the model top; (7) the surface boundary temperature tbound = tsk capped at 339.99 K (the Planck table limit) and the 16-band surface emissivity semiss = emiss. NOT in this component: the ozone column colo3, which MM5ATM takes from the O3DATA annual-mean climatology (31-bin layer-mean average of the summer/winter tables, INIRAD) evaluated on the EXTENDED column PZR -- a pressure-weighted mean of a piecewise-constant profile that will be written as an `integral` over pressure in the next pass (the dumped o3prof is the same climatology on the model column only and is not what colo3 uses; they differ by 33 %); the 1e-32 floors of SETCOEF on zero CO2/N2O/CH4 columns (never active with the WRF trace-gas inputs); and the cross-section species WX (all zero in WRF). NBUF is a metaparameter because RRTMINIT fixes it once from the model top, NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top/(100 deltap)) - 1, i.e. NBUF = nint(p_top/(100 deltap)); 44 for the reference column with p_top = 177.6 hPa. Inputs are REWRITE-TARGET ops `input_<name>` that the consumer lowers (in the inline tests through a per-test expression_template_imports library generated by tools/fill_tests.py). Ozone (added 2026-09-06): the annual-mean O3DATA climatology of MM5ATM/O3PROF2 as the layer integral of a piecewise-constant profile, including WRF's one-layer shift (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B5), and colo3.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "radiation",
      "longwave",
      "rrtm",
      "column",
      "wrf"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Mlawer, E. J., S. J. Taubman, P. D. Brown, M. J. Iacono, and S. A. Clough (1997). Radiative transfer for inhomogeneous atmospheres: RRTM, a validated correlated-k model for the longwave. J. Geophys. Res., 102(D14), 16663-16682.",
        "doi": "10.1029/97JD00237"
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF 4.8 phys/module_ra_rrtm.F: MM5ATM (lines 3739-4246: model layers 4094-4103, buffer layers 4128-4147, column amounts 4148-4160 and 4177-4185, clouds 4195-4207), SETCOEF (lines 4386-4391, COLxxx = 1.E-20*WKL), RRTMINIT line 6850 (NLAYERS)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
    },
    "NBUF": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 44,
      "description": "Number of buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top, nint(p_top / (100 deltap)) with deltap = 4 hPa (RRTMINIT: NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top*0.01/deltap) - 1); 44 for the reference column (p_top = 177.6 hPa)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "rlay": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "NLEV",
          "NBUF"
        ]
      }
    },
    "rlev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "NLEV",
          "NBUF",
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "bands": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 16
    },
    "o3nodes": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 31
    },
    "o3edges": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 32
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "RRTMColumn": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_thermo.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "./rrtm_ozone_climatology.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./rrtm_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "expression_templates": {
        "condensate_path": {
          "params": [
            "rho",
            "q",
            "dz",
            "g_per_kg"
          ],
          "description": "Condensate path of a layer in g/m^2, rho q dz (MM5ATM CLWP, CIWP).",
          "body": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "rho",
              "q",
              "dz",
              "g_per_kg"
            ]
          }
        },
        "precipitation_path": {
          "params": [
            "rho",
            "q",
            "dz",
            "rho_ref",
            "g_per_kg"
          ],
          "description": "Precipitation path of a layer in g/m^2 with MM5ATM's 0.75 power of the water content, ((rho q)/rho_ref)^0.75 rho_ref dz (PLWP, PIWP; rho_ref = 1 kg/m^3 makes the Fortran's implicit SI power law dimensionally explicit).",
          "body": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "rho",
                          "q"
                        ]
                      },
                      "rho_ref"
                    ]
                  },
                  0.75
                ]
              },
              "rho_ref",
              "dz",
              "g_per_kg"
            ]
          }
        },
        "model_or_buffer_layer": {
          "params": [
            "L",
            "model_value",
            "buffer_value"
          ],
          "description": "Case split of an RRTM-layer quantity between the model layers (L <= NLEV) and the buffer layers above the model top.",
          "body": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "<=",
                "args": [
                  "L",
                  "NLEV"
                ]
              },
              "model_value",
              "buffer_value"
            ]
          }
        },
        "model_layer_index": {
          "params": [
            "L"
          ],
          "description": "The model-layer index of RRTM layer L, clamped to NLEV so that a model-column gather stays in bounds when it is evaluated on a buffer layer (where the case split discards it).",
          "body": {
            "op": "min",
            "args": [
              "L",
              "NLEV"
            ]
          }
        },
        "model_level_index": {
          "params": [
            "j"
          ],
          "description": "The model-interface index of RRTM level j, clamped to NLEV + 1 for the same reason as model_layer_index.",
          "body": {
            "op": "min",
            "args": [
              "j",
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "NLEV",
                  1
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "level_mean": {
          "params": [
            "x",
            "L"
          ],
          "description": "Mean of a level quantity over the two levels bounding layer L, (x[L] + x[L+1])/2 (MM5ATM PAVEL/TAVEL of the buffer layers).",
          "body": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              0.5,
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "x",
                      "L"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "x",
                      {
                        "op": "+",
                        "args": [
                          "L",
                          1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "standard_atmosphere_temperature": {
          "params": [
            "p"
          ],
          "description": "MM5ATM's standard-atmosphere temperature T_std(p): linear interpolation in pressure of the 60-point TPROF (K) vs PPROF (hPa) table (1000 hPa .. 0.10 hPa, stored with the pressure axis ascending), clamped beyond the ends -- the Fortran clamps at 0.10 hPa, the only end the buffer layers reach (above 1000 hPa it would extrapolate linearly, impossible above the model top). Spelled as the esm-spec 9.5.3 lowered form interp.linear(data, axis, p) rather than as a `function_tables` entry with `table_lookup`, because the Rust array interpreter of EarthSciAST (inline-test path) does not lower table_lookup (unevaluable_operator, see data/eqwefic/esm-repro/rrtm/probe_table_lookup.esm).",
          "body": {
            "op": "fn",
            "name": "interp.linear",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": [
                  237.53,
                  239.87,
                  242.77,
                  245.46,
                  248.23,
                  251.07,
                  254.02,
                  256.49,
                  258.78,
                  260.85,
                  262.76,
                  264.45,
                  265.34,
                  265.42,
                  264.67,
                  263.38,
                  261.88,
                  259.84,
                  257.02,
                  254.04,
                  251.08,
                  248.13,
                  245.21,
                  242.3,
                  239.5,
                  236.82,
                  234.22,
                  231.88,
                  229.73,
                  227.78,
                  226.04,
                  224.39,
                  222.84,
                  221.31,
                  219.92,
                  218.89,
                  218.11,
                  217.42,
                  216.73,
                  215.96,
                  214.95,
                  213.81,
                  212.71,
                  211.73,
                  211.45,
                  211.63,
                  213.48,
                  215.21,
                  217.31,
                  220.52,
                  224.02,
                  228.78,
                  234.91,
                  241.97,
                  249.28,
                  256.71,
                  264.14,
                  270.73,
                  276.16,
                  279.94
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": [
                  0.1,
                  0.12,
                  0.14,
                  0.16,
                  0.19,
                  0.22,
                  0.26,
                  0.3,
                  0.35,
                  0.41,
                  0.48,
                  0.56,
                  0.65,
                  0.76,
                  0.89,
                  1.04,
                  1.22,
                  1.42,
                  1.66,
                  1.94,
                  2.27,
                  2.65,
                  3.1,
                  3.63,
                  4.24,
                  4.95,
                  5.79,
                  6.77,
                  7.91,
                  9.25,
                  10.81,
                  12.64,
                  14.77,
                  17.27,
                  20.19,
                  23.6,
                  27.59,
                  32.25,
                  37.69,
                  44.06,
                  51.51,
                  60.21,
                  70.38,
                  82.27,
                  96.17,
                  112.42,
                  131.41,
                  153.62,
                  179.57,
                  209.91,
                  245.38,
                  286.83,
                  335.29,
                  391.94,
                  458.16,
                  535.57,
                  626.05,
                  731.82,
                  855.47,
                  1000.0
                ]
              },
              "p"
            ]
          }
        },
        "climatology_layer_mean": {
          "params": [
            "p_bottom",
            "p_top"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure-weighted mean of the piecewise-constant annual ozone climatology over the interval [p_top, p_bottom] (p_bottom > p_top): (1/(p_bottom - p_top)) integral over p of o3_ann(p) dp, evaluated exactly as the sum over the 31 climatology bins [pp_half[j+1], pp_half[j]] of the overlap length max(0, min(p_bottom, pp_half[j]) - max(p_top, pp_half[j+1])) times the bin value o3_ann[j] (O3DATA loop 25: PB2 - PB1 - PT2 + PT1 is that overlap).",
          "body": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "args": [],
                "output_idx": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "j": {
                    "from": "o3nodes"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "max",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            0.0,
                            "par.unit_hpa"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "min",
                              "args": [
                                "p_bottom",
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pp_half",
                                    "j"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "max",
                              "args": [
                                "p_top",
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pp_half",
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        "j",
                                        1
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "o3_ann",
                        "j"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "p_bottom",
                  "p_top"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "co2vmr": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.000379,
          "description": "CO2 volume mixing ratio (WRF co2vmr from the trace-gas time series; 379 ppmv in the reference run)."
        },
        "n2ovmr": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 3.19e-07,
          "description": "N2O volume mixing ratio (WRF n2ovmr)."
        },
        "ch4vmr": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.774e-06,
          "description": "CH4 volume mixing ratio (WRF ch4vmr)."
        },
        "tsk": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 288.0,
          "description": "Surface skin temperature (WRF tsk)."
        },
        "emiss": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.92,
          "description": "Broadband surface emissivity (WRF emiss), applied to every RRTM band."
        },
        "p_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Model interface pressure (WRF p8w, bottom-up), consumer-supplied through `input_p_e`."
        },
        "T_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Model interface temperature (WRF t8w), consumer-supplied through `input_T_e`."
        },
        "p": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Model layer pressure (WRF p3d), consumer-supplied through `input_p`."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Model layer temperature (WRF t3d), consumer-supplied through `input_T`."
        },
        "qv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Water-vapour mixing ratio (WRF qv3d), consumer-supplied through `input_qv`."
        },
        "qc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio (WRF qc3d), consumer-supplied through `input_qc`."
        },
        "qr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Rain mixing ratio (WRF qr3d), consumer-supplied through `input_qr`."
        },
        "qi": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud-ice mixing ratio (WRF qi3d), consumer-supplied through `input_qi`."
        },
        "qs": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Snow mixing ratio (WRF qs3d), consumer-supplied through `input_qs`."
        },
        "cldfra": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Model cloud fraction (WRF cldfra3d), consumer-supplied through `input_cldfra`."
        },
        "dz_m": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Model layer thickness (WRF dz8w), consumer-supplied through `input_dz_m`."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Dry-air density p/(r_d T) of the model layers (MM5ATM RO)."
        },
        "clwp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud liquid water path of the model layer, rho qc dz (MM5ATM CLWP)."
        },
        "ciwp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud ice path rho qi dz (MM5ATM CIWP)."
        },
        "plwp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Rain path (rho qr)^0.75 dz (MM5ATM PLWP)."
        },
        "piwp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Snow path (rho qs)^0.75 dz (MM5ATM PIWP)."
        },
        "tau_model": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Longwave cloud optical depth of the model layer, abcw clwp + abice ciwp + abrn plwp + absn piwp (MM5ATM TAUCLOUD before the buffer extension)."
        },
        "pz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "shape": [
            "rlev"
          ],
          "description": "RRTM level pressure (MM5ATM PZ(0..NLAYERS)): the model interfaces p_e/100, then buffer levels descending by deltap, then 0 at the top of the column."
        },
        "tz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "rlev"
          ],
          "description": "RRTM level temperature (MM5ATM TZ): the model interface temperatures, then the shifted standard atmosphere T_std(pz) + (T_e[NLEV+1] - T_std(p_top))."
        },
        "pavel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "RRTM layer pressure (MM5ATM PAVEL): the model layer pressures p/100, then the buffer level means."
        },
        "tavel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "RRTM layer temperature (MM5ATM TAVEL): the model layer temperatures, then the buffer level means."
        },
        "w_h2o": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Water-vapour volume mixing ratio relative to dry air (MM5ATM WKL(1,L) before the COLDRY scaling): max(qv, qv_min) amdw in the model layers, h2ovmr_top above."
        },
        "amm": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/mol",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Molecular weight of the moist air of the layer, (1 - w_h2o) amd + w_h2o amw (MM5ATM amm)."
        },
        "coldry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Dry-air molecular column of the layer, (dp/g)(N_A/amm)/(1 + w_h2o) in molecules/cm^2 (MM5ATM COLDRY = (PZ(L-1)-PZ(L))*1.E3*avgdro/(gravit*amm*(1+WKL(1,L)))."
        },
        "colh2o": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled water-vapour column 1e-20 coldry w_h2o (SETCOEF COLH2O)."
        },
        "colco2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled CO2 column 1e-20 coldry co2vmr (SETCOEF COLCO2)."
        },
        "coln2o": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled N2O column 1e-20 coldry n2ovmr (SETCOEF COLN2O; MM5ATM multiplies by amdn and divides it out again)."
        },
        "colch4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled CH4 column 1e-20 coldry ch4vmr (SETCOEF COLCH4)."
        },
        "colo2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled O2 column: identically 0, because WRF's MM5ATM never fills WKL(7) (SETCOEF COLO2)."
        },
        "taucloud": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Longwave cloud optical depth of the RRTM layer: tau_model in the model layers, 0 above the model top (MM5ATM TAUCLOUD)."
        },
        "cldfrac": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud fraction of the RRTM layer: the model cloud fraction, forced to 1 where taucloud > tau_overcast, 0 above the model top (MM5ATM CLDFRAC)."
        },
        "tbound": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Surface boundary temperature for the Planck emission, tsk capped at tbound_reset when it exceeds tbound_limit (MM5ATM TBOUND)."
        },
        "semiss": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "bands"
          ],
          "description": "Surface emissivity of each of the 16 RRTM bands, all equal to emiss (MM5ATM SEMISS(N) = EMISS)."
        },
        "pp_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "shape": [
            "o3nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure nodes of the summer ozone climatology (O3DATA PPSUM), also the nodes of the annual mean (PPANN = PPSUM)."
        },
        "o3_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "o3nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Summer ozone mass mixing ratio at pp_sum (O3DATA O3SUM)."
        },
        "pp_win": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "shape": [
            "o3nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Pressure nodes of the winter ozone climatology (O3DATA PPWIN)."
        },
        "o3_win": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "o3nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Winter ozone mass mixing ratio at pp_win (O3DATA O3WIN)."
        },
        "o3_ann": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "o3nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Annual-mean ozone climatology at pp_sum (O3DATA O3ANN): the mean of the summer value and the winter profile interpolated linearly in pressure onto the summer node (for node 1 the plain mean of the two first values), exactly as O3DATA blends the two seasons."
        },
        "pp_half": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "shape": [
            "o3edges"
          ],
          "description": "Bin edges of the piecewise-constant annual climatology (O3DATA PPWRKH): 1100 hPa, the midpoints between successive nodes, and 0 hPa."
        },
        "o3_clim": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Ozone mass mixing ratio of the RRTM layer as MM5ATM assigns it (O3PROF2): the pressure-weighted mean of the piecewise-constant annual climatology, (1/dp) integral of o3_ann(p) dp, over the pressure interval MM5ATM passes to O3DATA. That interval is NOT the layer's own: MM5ATM reverses PZ(1..NLAYERS) without PZ(0) into the array O3DATA reads, so layer L receives the mean over [PZ(L+1), PZ(L)] = [pz[L+2], pz[L+1]] -- the layer above it -- and the top layer receives the constant 6.135e-6 (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B5). The integral is evaluated exactly as the sum over climatology bins of the overlap of the interval with each bin times the bin value (O3DATA's PB/PT bookkeeping)."
        },
        "o3_clim_own_layer": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "The same climatological mean evaluated over the layer's own pressure interval [pz[L+1], pz[L]]: what O3DATA is meant to return. Not what WRF uses (see o3_clim); provided so the magnitude of the off-by-one shift is visible (27 % of the column maximum in the reference column). Not asserted against the Fortran."
        },
        "colo3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/cm^2",
          "shape": [
            "rlay"
          ],
          "description": "Scaled ozone column 1e-20 coldry o3_clim amdo (SETCOEF COLO3 from MM5ATM WKL(3,L) = O3PROF2(L) amdo COLDRY)."
        }
      },
