        {
          "id": "scm_call120_thick_overcast",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NBUF = 44 buffer layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_ref2_120.json). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, COLO3, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of tile column 1 (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 2e-4, colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7 cm^-2; colo3 1e-7; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise, and identities on the inputs (tbound, semiss) use rel 1e-9. This regime is one of the four added on 2026-09-06 to cover MM5ATM's cloud block (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4255): TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP on the model layers and zero on the buffer layers, and the overcast override IF (TAUCLOUD > 0.01) CLDFRC = 1, which replaces the diagnosed cloud fraction of every optically thicker layer by 1 and is the reason RTRN can only ever see 0 < CLDFRAC < 1 in a layer whose cloud optical depth is at or below 0.01. Regime: OVERCAST, optically thick. Call 120, 20:00 UTC (13:34 LST), the deepest cirrus deck of the run (ice only: qc = qr = qs = qg = 0 throughout, qi up to 4.6e-5 kg/kg in layers 51-57). TAUCLOUD = 0.0542, 0.636, 0.760, 0.467, 0.233, 0.0837, 0.0238 there, all above the 0.01 threshold, so the diagnosed CLDFRA 0.0212, 0.561, 0.976, 0.996, 1, 1, 1 is overridden to CLDFRAC = 1 in all seven layers -- the override fires on four of them, including one whose diagnosed fraction is only 2 %. tsk = 285.69 K. Measured mismatch: pz and pavel to Linf 2.9e-5 hPa (the real32 Pa -> hPa division), tz to 2.9e-5 K and tavel to 2.2e-5 K, coldry to 1.1e18 cm^-2 and the column amounts to 3.7e-6 relative (colh2o Linf 3.3e-5, colco2 4.1e-6, coln2o 3.6e-9, colch4 2.0e-8, colo3 2.7e-8 cm^-2), CLDFRAC and COLO2 exactly, and TAUCLOUD to Linf 7.8e-8 on a column maximum of 0.760 (1e-7 relative), so this regime's taucloud tolerance is abs 1e-6 rather than the 1e-8 of the optically thin regimes -- 13x the measured floor and still 1e-6 of the column maximum.",
