        {
          "id": "scm_call648_fractional_overlap",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NBUF = 44 buffer layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_cloud_648.json, written by the same em_scm_xy run re-executed for 8 h with the cloudy calls added to ESM_DUMP_CALLS; the re-run reproduces the archived call 120 dump bit-for-bit, so it is the same trajectory). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, COLO3, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of tile column 1 (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 2e-4, colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7 cm^-2; colo3 1e-7; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise, and identities on the inputs (tbound, semiss) use rel 1e-9. This regime is one of the four added on 2026-09-06 to cover MM5ATM's cloud block (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4255): TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP on the model layers and zero on the buffer layers, and the overcast override IF (TAUCLOUD > 0.01) CLDFRC = 1, which replaces the diagnosed cloud fraction of every optically thicker layer by 1 and is the reason RTRN can only ever see 0 < CLDFRAC < 1 in a layer whose cloud optical depth is at or below 0.01. Regime: MULTI-LAYER OVERLAP. Call 648, 00:24 UTC (17:58 LST), thin residual cirrus. Layer 51 has condensate (TAUCLOUD = 0.00314) but CLDFRA = 0 and stays cloud-free because the override is not triggered; layer 52 is overridden from 0.0594 to 1 (TAUCLOUD = 0.0237); layers 53, 54, 55 keep their diagnosed fractions 0.0698, 0.0194, 0.0387 (TAUCLOUD 0.00983, 0.00160, 0.00152); layers 56, 57, 59 are diagnosed overcast. Three adjacent fractional layers between a clear and an overcast one, the input of the RTRNSweep test scm_call648_fractional_overlap. tsk = 281.17 K. Measured mismatch: pz and pavel to Linf 2.9e-5 hPa, tz to 2.9e-5 K and tavel to 2.2e-5 K, coldry to 1.0e18 cm^-2 and the column amounts to 1.4e-6 relative (colh2o Linf 4.0e-5, colco2 3.9e-6, coln2o 3.1e-9, colch4 1.8e-8, colo3 2.7e-8 cm^-2), CLDFRAC exactly -- the clear layer 51 with condensate, the overridden layer 52 and the three fractional layers 53-55 -- and TAUCLOUD to Linf 1.6e-9 on a column maximum of 0.0237, so taucloud uses abs 2e-8 (13x the measured floor).",
