          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 idealized supercell (em_quarter_ss, Weisman-Klemp sounding, 41 x 41 x 59 mass points, dx = 2 km, dt = 6 s, ztop = 12800 m so p_top = 177.07 hPa and NBUF = nint(p_top/4 hPa) = 44 -- the same 59 + 44 = 103-layer RRTM column as the em_scm_xy regimes, because esm inline tests cannot override the NLEV/NBUF metaparameters) with mp=6 (WSM6), ra_lw=1 (RRTM), ra_sw=1 (Dudhia), radt = 5 min and no surface/PBL scheme, run for 1 h and dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, GNU real32 build). The RRTM hook dumps one j-row per call, so call = (nrad - 1) * 41 + j, and the new ESM_DUMP_I selector picks which tile column's MM5ATM/SETCOEF/RTRN internals are written; here column i = 20. RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, COLO3, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of that column (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 1.5e-3 -- the supercell column holds 131 cm^-2, six times the SCM's, so this one is scaled up from the SCM regimes' 2e-4; colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7, colo3 1e-7 cm^-2; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), and the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise. This regime exists to exercise the three terms of MM5ATM's cloud optical depth (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4253) that the em_scm_xy reference case leaves at zero: TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP with ABCW = 0.144, ABICE = 0.0735, ABRN = 0.330e-3, ABSN = 2.34e-3 -- the SCM run is ice-only (qc = qr = qs = qg = 0 for all 59 h), so only ABICE was ever verified. Regime: WARM LIQUID CLOUD, the pure ABCW case. Call 61 (nrad = 2, model time 00:05:00, j = 20, i = 20): the first convective thermal of the run, entirely above freezing (T = 274.1-284.1 K in the cloud) and entirely liquid -- qi = qr = qs = qg = 0 EVERYWHERE in the column, qc up to 2.186e-4 kg/kg in RRTM layers 10-15, so TAUCLOUD = ABCW CLWP alone there and nowhere else. TAUCLOUD = 1.262, 3.825, 6.107, 6.430, 4.409, 1.351 in layers 10-15 and 0 in the other 97; a wrong ABCW moves every one of those six numbers proportionally, and no other coefficient can compensate. The diagnosed CLDFRA there is 0.423-0.988, all above the 0.01 optical-depth threshold, so MM5ATM's IF (TAUCLOUD > 0.01) CLDFRC = 1 override (N58) forces CLDFRAC = 1 in all six -- the liquid twin of the ice overcast regime at SCM call 120. tsk = 299.97 K, emiss = 0.85. Measured mismatch: pz and pavel to Linf 2.9e-5 hPa (the real32 Pa -> hPa division), tz to 2.3e-5 K and tavel to 1.8e-5 K, coldry to 1.1e18 cm^-2, colh2o to 1.8e-4, colco2 to 4.1e-6, coln2o to 3.6e-9, colch4 to 1.9e-8 and colo3 to 2.8e-8 cm^-2, CLDFRAC and COLO2 exactly, and TAUCLOUD to Linf 8.5e-7 on a column maximum of 6.430 (1.4e-7 relative at worst), so this regime's taucloud tolerance is abs 1e-5 -- 12x the measured floor and 1.6e-6 of the column maximum, the same fraction the SCM regimes use -- and the six per-layer spot checks use the contract rel 1e-5, 70x their measured floor.",
