        {
          "id": "qss_call268_mixed_phase_storm",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 idealized supercell (em_quarter_ss, Weisman-Klemp sounding, 41 x 41 x 59 mass points, dx = 2 km, dt = 6 s, ztop = 12800 m so p_top = 177.07 hPa and NBUF = nint(p_top/4 hPa) = 44 -- the same 59 + 44 = 103-layer RRTM column as the em_scm_xy regimes, because esm inline tests cannot override the NLEV/NBUF metaparameters) with mp=6 (WSM6), ra_lw=1 (RRTM), ra_sw=1 (Dudhia), radt = 5 min and no surface/PBL scheme, run for 1 h and dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, GNU real32 build). The RRTM hook dumps one j-row per call, so call = (nrad - 1) * 41 + j, and the new ESM_DUMP_I selector picks which tile column's MM5ATM/SETCOEF/RTRN internals are written; here column i = 20. RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, COLO3, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of that column (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 1.5e-3 -- the supercell column holds 131 cm^-2, six times the SCM's, so this one is scaled up from the SCM regimes' 2e-4; colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7, colo3 1e-7 cm^-2; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), and the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise. This regime exists to exercise the three terms of MM5ATM's cloud optical depth (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4253) that the em_scm_xy reference case leaves at zero: TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP with ABCW = 0.144, ABICE = 0.0735, ABRN = 0.330e-3, ABSN = 2.34e-3 -- the SCM run is ice-only (qc = qr = qs = qg = 0 for all 59 h), so only ABICE was ever verified. Regime: MIXED-PHASE STORM COLUMN, all four terms at once. Call 268 (nrad = 7, model time 00:30:00, j = 22, i = 20): a mature supercell column, cloudy in 57 of the 59 model layers, with qc <= 8.4e-4, qr <= 1.05e-2, qi <= 1.05e-4 and qs <= 8.2e-5 kg/kg. TAUCLOUD rises to 18.74 and every one of the four terms dominates somewhere in the column, which is what makes each coefficient separately observable: layers 1-10 are pure rain (qc = qi = qs = 0, TAUCLOUD = 0.3996 at layer 1 and 2.384 at layer 8 = ABRN PLWP alone); layers 11-19 are liquid + rain (layer 12: 1.199 from ABCW and 2.329 from ABRN, TAUCLOUD = 3.528); layers 22-33 carry all four (layer 24: 17.56 + 0.0161 + 1.160 + 0.00138 = 18.73); layers 39-41 are pure ice (layer 39: 0.7676 = ABICE CIWP alone); and layers 51-54 are snow-dominated (layer 52: 5.759e-2, of which the snow term is 5.759e-2 and the ice term only 5.4e-6, i.e. 99.99 % ABSN; layer 54 splits 1.128e-2 ice against 1.253e-2 snow). Layer 56 is the one layer the CLDFRC override leaves alone (TAUCLOUD = 4.81e-3 < 0.01), so CLDFRAC = 0.0110 survives into RTRN, while layer 55 at TAUCLOUD = 1.311e-2 is forced from 0.031 to 1. tsk = 300.02 K, emiss = 0.85. Measured mismatch: pz to Linf 2.7e-5 hPa and pavel to 2.9e-5 hPa (the real32 Pa -> hPa division), tz to 2.3e-5 K and tavel to 1.8e-5 K, coldry to 1.1e18 cm^-2, colh2o to 1.8e-4, colco2 to 4.3e-6, coln2o to 3.5e-9, colch4 to 2.0e-8 and colo3 to 2.7e-8 cm^-2, CLDFRAC and COLO2 exactly, and TAUCLOUD to Linf 3.1e-6 on a column maximum of 18.74 (1.3e-7 relative at worst and <= 4.6e-8 at each of the eight spot-check layers), so this regime's taucloud tolerance is abs 3e-5 -- 10x the measured floor and 1.6e-6 of the column maximum -- and the spot checks use the contract rel 1e-5, 200x their measured floor. Graupel reaches 6.2e-4 kg/kg here and contributes nothing: MM5ATM takes QG as an argument and never uses it (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N62).",
