        {
          "id": "qss_call396_ice_snow_anvil",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 idealized supercell (em_quarter_ss, Weisman-Klemp sounding, 41 x 41 x 59 mass points, dx = 2 km, dt = 6 s, ztop = 12800 m so p_top = 177.07 hPa and NBUF = nint(p_top/4 hPa) = 44 -- the same 59 + 44 = 103-layer RRTM column as the em_scm_xy regimes, because esm inline tests cannot override the NLEV/NBUF metaparameters) with mp=6 (WSM6), ra_lw=1 (RRTM), ra_sw=1 (Dudhia), radt = 5 min and no surface/PBL scheme, run for 1 h and dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, GNU real32 build). The RRTM hook dumps one j-row per call, so call = (nrad - 1) * 41 + j, and the new ESM_DUMP_I selector picks which tile column's MM5ATM/SETCOEF/RTRN internals are written; here column i = 40. RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, COLO3, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of that column (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 1.5e-3 -- the supercell column holds 131 cm^-2, six times the SCM's, so this one is scaled up from the SCM regimes' 2e-4; colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7, colo3 1e-7 cm^-2; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), and the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise. This regime exists to exercise the three terms of MM5ATM's cloud optical depth (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4253) that the em_scm_xy reference case leaves at zero: TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP with ABCW = 0.144, ABICE = 0.0735, ABRN = 0.330e-3, ABSN = 2.34e-3 -- the SCM run is ice-only (qc = qr = qs = qg = 0 for all 59 h), so only ABICE was ever verified. Regime: ICE-AND-SNOW ANVIL, the pure ABSN/ABICE case. Call 396 (nrad = 10, model time 00:45:00, j = 27, i = 40): the downshear anvil of the supercell, 40 km from the updraft, with no liquid water and no rain anywhere in the column below 645 hPa (qc = 0 and qr <= 1.1e-6 kg/kg everywhere, so the ABCW and ABRN terms are identically zero except for a 2.3e-3 residue at layer 16), qi up to 1.18e-4 and qs up to 3.4e-4 kg/kg. This is the regime that pins ABSN: RRTM layers 17-30 hold snow and NOTHING else (qc = qr = qi = 0), so TAUCLOUD = ABSN PIWP alone there -- 0.0466, 0.1688, 0.0860 and 0.4652 at layers 17, 20, 27 and 30 -- while layers 51-53 hold ice and nothing else (TAUCLOUD = 2.04e-3 at layer 53 = ABICE CIWP alone), and layers 33-47 mix the two in every proportion (layer 41: 0.8016 ice against 0.1489 snow; layer 33: 0.0308 ice against 0.4654 snow, 94 % snow). Cloud fraction: layer 52 is one of the rare layers whose optical depth stays under MM5ATM's 0.01 threshold (TAUCLOUD = 9.59e-3), so its diagnosed CLDFRA = 0.0287 survives into CLDFRAC, while layer 51 at 2.69e-2 is forced from 0.0852 to 1 and layer 26, whose diagnosed CLDFRA is 0 exactly, is forced to 1 by TAUCLOUD = 1.74e-2 (N58). tsk = 299.97 K, emiss = 0.85. Measured mismatch: pz and pavel to Linf 2.9e-5 hPa (the real32 Pa -> hPa division), tz to 2.3e-5 K and tavel to 1.7e-5 K, coldry to 1.2e18 cm^-2, colh2o to 2.5e-4, colco2 to 4.6e-6, coln2o to 4.0e-9, colch4 to 2.1e-8 and colo3 to 2.8e-8 cm^-2, CLDFRAC and COLO2 exactly, and TAUCLOUD to Linf 6.4e-8 on a column maximum of 1.0438 (1.3e-7 relative at worst over the nine spot-check layers), so this regime's taucloud tolerance is abs 1e-6 -- 16x the measured floor and 1e-6 of the column maximum -- and the nine per-layer spot checks use the contract rel 1e-5, 75x their measured floor.",
